WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:07.574
 NARRATOR: Egypt, the richest
 source of archaeological
 treasures on the planet.

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:13.179
SALIMA: Oh, that's
a fabulous one!

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:19.185
 NARRATOR: Beneath this desert
 landscape lie the secrets
 of this ancient civilization.

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:24.824
JOHN: Wow, you can see why
the pharaohs chose this place.

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:31.031
 NARRATOR: Now, for a full
 season of excavations, our
 cameras have unprecedented

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:36.803
 access to follow teams on the
 frontline of archaeology...

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:40.306
ASHRAF: I'm driving so fast
because I'm so excited!

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.942
KATHLEEN: It's an entrance,
we can see an entrance.

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:46.913
 NARRATOR: Revealing
 buried secrets...

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:49.816
ANTONIO: I have just
been told that they
have found something.

00:00:50.282 --> 00:00:51.951
DON: Oh my gosh.

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:54.020
(laughs).

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:55.822
JOHN: A sphinx!

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:01.594
 NARRATOR: And making
 discoveries that could
 rewrite ancient history.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:12.238
 This time, the hunt for the
 lost tomb of Queen Cleopatra.

00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:17.410
 Colleen searches for clues
 in the hieroglyphs...

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:20.580
COLLEEN: Here we see
Cleopatra as the goddess Isis.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:25.652
 NARRATOR: Alejandro
 scans ancient mummies in
 an Egyptian hospital...

00:01:29.955 --> 00:01:33.560
 NARRATOR: And
 Kathleen makes a startling
 discovery deep underground.

00:01:51.443 --> 00:01:56.950
 NARRATOR: Ancient Egypt,
 a kingdom of great pharaohs
 and a cradle of civilization.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:06.759
 But after 3,000 years
 this rule came to an
 end with the last pharaoh,

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:11.164
 Queen Cleopatra.

00:02:13.098 --> 00:02:18.338
 For centuries this enigmatic
 woman has captured the
 imagination of the world,

00:02:20.272 --> 00:02:24.878
 but the location of her
 tomb is still a mystery.

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:32.785
 Today archaeologists
 across Egypt are on
 the hunt for clues.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:41.261
 Renowned Egyptologists Colleen
 and John Darnell are experts
 in decoding hieroglyphs,

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:46.099
 they're on their way to
 the Valley of the Kings.

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:48.935
COLLEEN: We're headed to the
location of the burials of

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.337
nearly every pharaoh
of the New Kingdom.

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:57.010
 NARRATOR: The Valley
 is a rabbit warren of
 sixty-five hidden tombs.

00:02:57.843 --> 00:03:01.915
 They form one of the
 greatest royal
 cemeteries in the world,

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:04.817
 but not all of
 them are finished.

00:03:05.751 --> 00:03:10.390
JOHN: This morning we're
going to the unfinished
tomb of Ramses XI.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:17.463
It's the last tomb begun in
the Valley of the Kings, and
many times unfinished things

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:21.501
in Egypt can actually tell
you a little bit more than
the completed product.

00:03:26.772 --> 00:03:31.811
 NARRATOR: Ramses XI
 reigned over 1,000
 years before Cleopatra,

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:36.716
 but when he died his
 tomb was never used.

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:42.789
COLLEEN: So here you could
see just the initial phases
of the tomb decoration,

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:46.259
but it's already a beautiful
depiction of Ramses XI.

00:03:46.992 --> 00:03:50.897
We know exactly who we're
looking at because of his
cartouches, his name rings,

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:54.067
in front of his face.

00:03:54.266 --> 00:03:58.771
JOHN: Looks like they've
laid out what would've been
remarkable illustrations and,

00:03:58.804 --> 00:04:02.275
and texts early in the
initial part of the tomb.

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:09.548
 NARRATOR: The tomb of
 Ramses XI is located in
 the east of the

00:04:09.581 --> 00:04:12.552
 Valley of the Kings.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:18.157
 Its cavernous chambers
 and pillared halls reveal
 how the pharaoh should

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:24.563
 have been buried,
 but the back of the
 tomb is unfinished.

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:32.839
 After 500 years
 of Egypt's kings and queens
 being buried in the Valley,

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:37.477
 Ramses' tomb marks
 the end of an era.

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:44.216
 Ramses XI abandoned
 the Valley of the Kings,

00:04:44.249 --> 00:04:47.820
 and no more pharaohs
 were buried here.

00:04:48.153 --> 00:04:53.092
COLLEEN: This is very much the
end of a legacy, this is the
end of kings being buried in

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:55.661
the Valley of the Kings,
but it's also the start of
something new,

00:04:55.694 --> 00:04:59.832
of continued royal burial
that really ends with Cleopatra.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:07.140
 NARRATOR: Historians believe
 this royal burial site was
 abandoned because of looting,

00:05:07.806 --> 00:05:12.144
 but no one has found the
 cemetery for the last
 pharaohs of Egypt,

00:05:12.177 --> 00:05:14.981
 Cleopatra and
 her family line.

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:19.319
 So where could it be?

00:05:20.285 --> 00:05:23.789
 After the Valley fell out
 of use eventually Egypt's

00:05:23.822 --> 00:05:26.726
 seat of power
 shifted north to Alexandria.

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:40.639
 The last great dynasty of
 pharaohs established their
 capital here to exploit

00:05:40.672 --> 00:05:43.676
 trade across
 the Mediterranean Sea.

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:49.182
 Archaeologist Dr. Ross Thomas
 from the British Museum
 is here exploring the ancient

00:05:49.648 --> 00:05:53.219
 capital for evidence that
 could lead to Cleopatra.

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:58.558
ROSS: The ancient city housed
about half a million people
during the first century BC

00:05:59.391 --> 00:06:01.861
and it was one of the most
important ancient ports

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:04.897
and ancient cities
of the Mediterranean.

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:10.302
 NARRATOR: The port city
 of Alexandria was founded
 by Alexander the Great

00:06:10.335 --> 00:06:13.172
 who conquered Egypt
 2,300 years ago.

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:21.013
 It was famed for its palaces,
 statues, its library, and a
 colossal lighthouse standing

00:06:21.747 --> 00:06:26.285
 over 350 feet tall, one
 of the seven wonders
 of the ancient world.

00:06:29.621 --> 00:06:33.593
 During this time,
 Egypt was ruled by the
 successors of Alexander,

00:06:34.092 --> 00:06:36.829
 the Greek pharaohs
 called the Ptolemies,

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:43.669
 but this family line ended
 when the country was eventually
 conquered by Rome,

00:06:44.136 --> 00:06:48.141
 leaving the last pharaoh
 of Egypt Queen Cleopatra.

00:06:53.645 --> 00:06:58.551
 Many archaeologists think
 Cleopatra will be found in a
 royal cemetery somewhere in

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:02.121
 Alexandria, the capital
 built by her own family...

00:07:04.089 --> 00:07:06.893
 but searching
 here is difficult.

00:07:07.392 --> 00:07:10.963
 The ancient city was hit by
 a series of earthquakes and

00:07:10.996 --> 00:07:14.133
 much of it now
 lies beneath the waves.

00:07:14.433 --> 00:07:16.202
ROSS: So do we
have weights here?

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:18.171
MAN: Yes.

00:07:22.241 --> 00:07:27.146
 NARRATOR: Professor
 Emad Khalil from Alexandria
 University began exploring

00:07:27.179 --> 00:07:32.218
 the sunken city over twenty
 years ago, keeping an eagle
 eye out for Cleopatra's tomb.

00:07:34.119 --> 00:07:36.889
EMAD: This has not been found
obviously in Alexandria yet,

00:07:36.922 --> 00:07:41.694
but as we always say
beneath Alexandria there
are other Alexandrias.

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:45.932
Okay.

00:07:51.436 --> 00:07:56.476
 NARRATOR: The evidence of
 Cleopatra's ancient capital
 is strewn across the seabed.

00:07:58.677 --> 00:08:03.316
 Shards of pottery,
 huge columns,

00:08:07.319 --> 00:08:11.991
 fallen obelisks,
 and what they believe is one

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:14.927
 of the doorways to
 the famous lighthouse.

00:08:23.435 --> 00:08:29.809
ROSS: There was scores of
columns and column bases,
hundreds of blocks,

00:08:31.043 --> 00:08:33.112
really large
structural blocks.

00:08:33.145 --> 00:08:35.748
EMAD: I think we managed
to see a part of an obelisk,

00:08:35.781 --> 00:08:38.317
and part of a
doorway of the lighthouse,

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:40.386
so it is, it's really,
really something.

00:08:41.086 --> 00:08:42.621
ROSS: Yeah.

00:08:42.654 --> 00:08:46.425
 NARRATOR: Every
 dive provides new data for
 Emad and Ross to research,

00:08:46.458 --> 00:08:49.762
 but there's no
 sign of Cleopatra or
 her family's graves.

00:08:50.462 --> 00:08:53.833
EMAD: Well you'd assume
that they'd want to be
buried in their own city.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:58.170
Normally what you
have is a royal cemetery
with all the burials

00:08:58.203 --> 00:09:00.306
for the kings and queens.

00:09:02.274 --> 00:09:05.745
 NARRATOR: But what if
 Cleopatra wasn't buried
 in Alexandria at all?

00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:10.950
 One woman thinks
 everyone has been looking
 in the wrong place.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:19.525
 Thirty miles west of
 Alexandria in an ancient city
 called Taposiris Magna,

00:09:20.993 --> 00:09:23.496
 there is a
 little-known temple.

00:09:23.795 --> 00:09:29.669
 Here Kathleen Martinez,
 a qualified lawyer turned
 archaeologist, is on a quest.

00:09:31.236 --> 00:09:34.373
KATHLEEN: So this is one
of the exciting moments
of an excavation.

00:09:35.707 --> 00:09:40.713
 NARRATOR: For the past decade
 she has been building a case
 that Queen Cleopatra is buried

00:09:41.313 --> 00:09:43.882
 beneath this temple.

00:09:43.915 --> 00:09:47.086
KATHLEEN: I want to
be an archaeologist
since I was a child,

00:09:47.953 --> 00:09:53.292
but my parents convinced
me to study law, and I
became a lawyer.

00:09:55.727 --> 00:10:01.834
But all this knowledge and
this information that I had
as a lawyer I combine with

00:10:01.867 --> 00:10:06.472
archaeology, and this is
how I follow Cleopatra's
steps to Taposiris Magna.

00:10:08.774 --> 00:10:13.278
 NARRATOR: Kathleen is from
 the Dominican Republic in the
 Caribbean, but thirteen years

00:10:13.311 --> 00:10:18.084
 ago she gave up her law
 work and started excavating
 here at the temple.

00:10:19.084 --> 00:10:25.191
KATHLEEN: We have uncovered so
many important structures that
prove this temple functioned

00:10:25.691 --> 00:10:29.462
as a temple during the
time of Queen Cleopatra
and the Greek pharaohs.

00:10:30.095 --> 00:10:33.966
So this could be
the perfect place for
Cleopatra's lost tomb.

00:10:36.435 --> 00:10:40.105
 NARRATOR: At the age of
 eighteen, Cleopatra became
 pharaoh when her father

00:10:40.138 --> 00:10:42.508
 Ptolemy the twelfth died.

00:10:42.541 --> 00:10:45.378
 She went on to rule
 for twenty-one years.

00:10:45.944 --> 00:10:50.349
 Faced with the threat of a
 Roman invasion, she formed
 alliances with the enemy,

00:10:51.249 --> 00:10:54.153
 first wooing Julius Caesar
 and bearing his child,

00:10:55.253 --> 00:10:58.824
 followed by a
 relationship with Mark Antony.

00:10:59.291 --> 00:11:04.397
 But in 31 BC
 the Roman navy, led by
 Octavian, attacked Egypt.

00:11:08.133 --> 00:11:12.805
 To avoid capture, legend
 has it that Cleopatra
 committed suicide with

00:11:12.838 --> 00:11:16.008
 the bite of
 a venomous snake.

00:11:22.814 --> 00:11:26.118
KATHLEEN: She threatened Rome
and Romans were afraid of her.

00:11:26.151 --> 00:11:30.256
She thought she could
conquer the world, even
though she was a woman.

00:11:31.156 --> 00:11:36.495
She was a warrior, and she
achieved the impossible, and
this is why she is my heroine

00:11:37.596 --> 00:11:41.600
and I will try to
do everything I can
to find her tomb.

00:11:42.701 --> 00:11:46.572
 NARRATOR: Kathleen believes
 Cleopatra could be buried
 somewhere around the site.

00:11:48.073 --> 00:11:53.412
 This season, she has
 a promising lead 300 feet
 outside the temple walls;

00:11:54.613 --> 00:11:57.349
 a strange
 hollow in the ground.

00:11:57.382 --> 00:12:00.886
KATHLEEN: We found
a cut, it's a cut in the
bedrock, it's a shaft,

00:12:00.919 --> 00:12:04.790
and we are trying to find
out what, where it lead us.

00:12:05.791 --> 00:12:10.496
 NARRATOR: Kathleen believes
 the shaft could lead to
 Cleopatra's lost tomb,

00:12:10.529 --> 00:12:15.101
 hidden deep underground,
 but trying to excavate
 this site is dangerous.

00:12:20.438 --> 00:12:24.610
KATHLEEN: It's dangerous
because if the bucket turned
around it could hit the guys

00:12:25.143 --> 00:12:27.246
which are down there.

00:12:27.279 --> 00:12:30.916
 NARRATOR: With the potential
 to break through into an
 underground cavity,

00:12:30.949 --> 00:12:34.920
 they're worried the
 floor of the shaft
 could suddenly collapse.

00:12:42.561 --> 00:12:45.798
KATHLEEN: It's an entrance,
we can see an entrance.

00:12:46.164 --> 00:12:48.167
 NARRATOR: It's a
 huge discovery.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.170
 The shaft leads to an
 underground tunnel.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:52.805
KATHLEEN: It's so exciting.

00:12:52.838 --> 00:12:54.706
I need to see
what is in there.

00:12:54.739 --> 00:12:58.344
It has been hidden
for 2,000 years.

00:13:05.617 --> 00:13:10.089
 NARRATOR: Across Egypt, the
 hunt for lost tombs continues.

00:13:12.624 --> 00:13:17.196
 500 miles south of Alexandria
 is the ancient city of Aswan.

00:13:18.897 --> 00:13:23.402
 It's here that
 Spanish archaeologist
 Alejandro Jiménez-Serrano

00:13:23.435 --> 00:13:27.272
 leads a large
 mission working at
 the ancient necropolis

00:13:27.305 --> 00:13:29.775
 of Qubbet el-Hawa.

00:13:29.808 --> 00:13:34.246
 The site is home to one
 of the largest sets of
 intact tombs in Egypt.

00:13:34.946 --> 00:13:39.285
 Alejandro is
 searching for unmarked
 graves and lost tombs.

00:13:41.152 --> 00:13:43.422
(speaking in native language).

00:13:44.789 --> 00:13:50.596
 This sprawling site is even
 older than the Valley of the
 Kings, and is thought to be

00:13:50.629 --> 00:13:53.599
 the burial site of
 many wealthy nobles.

00:13:53.632 --> 00:13:59.538
 Today he's working in one of
 the ancient tombs, trying to
 identify who was buried there.

00:14:00.171 --> 00:14:04.243
ALEJANDRO: Unfortunately,
it has no inscriptions so we
don't the owner or the family

00:14:04.809 --> 00:14:06.645
who occupy this tomb.

00:14:06.678 --> 00:14:10.749
We can only say which period,
when it was built,

00:14:10.782 --> 00:14:13.552
because of the style.

00:14:19.391 --> 00:14:24.697
 NARRATOR: But deep inside
 this tomb the team has just
 unearthed two buried mummies.

00:14:27.399 --> 00:14:31.036
 As they clear away the
 sand, Alejandro makes
 a startling discovery;

00:14:34.472 --> 00:14:38.043
 it's the edge of a beautiful
 golden death mask.

00:14:39.177 --> 00:14:41.247
ALEJANDRO: Wow!

00:14:44.115 --> 00:14:49.688
 NARRATOR: Death masks are
 often made of layers of linen
 or recycled papyrus, and then

00:14:49.721 --> 00:14:52.691
 soaked in plaster.

00:14:52.958 --> 00:14:57.296
 This forms a tough
 material a bit like paper
 mache, called cartonnage.

00:15:01.399 --> 00:15:05.437
 While still wet, the
 cartonnage is molded to
 resemble the face of the

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:08.473
 deceased, and then painted.

00:15:08.506 --> 00:15:12.678
 Often the name of the person
 was written on the mask, along
 with inscriptions to help

00:15:13.278 --> 00:15:15.648
 transport the deceased
 into the afterlife.

00:15:18.249 --> 00:15:23.555
 This ancient funeral
 practice continued for
 over 2,000 years,

00:15:23.588 --> 00:15:26.926
 right up to
 the time of Cleopatra.

00:15:31.062 --> 00:15:34.733
ALEJANDRO: And the quality
of the cartonnage is,
is amazing, the, the colors,

00:15:34.766 --> 00:15:40.205
and it has text and it seems
that it will be possible to read
the name of the original owner.

00:15:41.606 --> 00:15:45.244
 NARRATOR: But before
 Alejandro can try to put
 a name to this ancient body,

00:15:46.111 --> 00:15:48.981
 his team will need
 to extract the fragile mask.

00:15:50.648 --> 00:15:56.822
 They use soft paintbrushes
 to remove the sand grain by
 grain, and then strengthen the

00:15:57.489 --> 00:16:01.827
 mask with paper
 coated with resin to
 stop it from breaking.

00:16:07.298 --> 00:16:12.771
ALEJANDRO: It's a privilege
and it's amazing to, to have
the opportunity to,

00:16:14.305 --> 00:16:18.811
to work with untouched material.

00:16:21.946 --> 00:16:24.717
 NARRATOR: Back at
 Taposiris Magna...

00:16:24.916 --> 00:16:27.486
KATHLEEN: They take
such good care of me.

00:16:28.887 --> 00:16:31.557
They are not used to women
going down the shaft.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:35.928
 NARRATOR: Kathleen
 Martinez is descending into
 a 2,000-year-old shaft.

00:16:38.663 --> 00:16:40.332
KATHLEEN: Yes.
Going down.

00:16:40.365 --> 00:16:44.336
 NARRATOR: She believes it
 could lead her to the lost
 tomb of Queen Cleopatra.

00:16:48.473 --> 00:16:50.675
 But there's a problem.

00:16:50.708 --> 00:16:54.380
KATHLEEN: God! The
tunnels are full of water.

00:16:56.147 --> 00:17:01.120
 NARRATOR: The vertical shaft
 descends twenty-feet down and
 leads to two narrow tunnels.

00:17:02.053 --> 00:17:07.359
KATHLEEN: We have tunnel
which is perfectly
cut in the bedrock.

00:17:08.359 --> 00:17:14.767
One it seems to lead
to the north, and the
other goes to the south.

00:17:21.239 --> 00:17:25.243
 NARRATOR: The fact that the
 tunnels are flooded makes
 any further exploration very

00:17:25.276 --> 00:17:28.580
 difficult, but Kathleen
 is determined to push on.

00:17:29.447 --> 00:17:31.016
KATHLEEN: Okay, look.

00:17:31.049 --> 00:17:33.552
Oh God, so creepy, look!

00:17:34.452 --> 00:17:38.424
At the end of the
tunnel there is a door,

00:17:40.959 --> 00:17:44.696
but it's almost completely
covered with water.

00:17:44.996 --> 00:17:48.600
 NARRATOR: Now she
 can see the quality of the
 stonework and how much effort

00:17:48.633 --> 00:17:51.536
 it would've taken to create
 these tunnels.

00:17:51.569 --> 00:17:55.407
 Kathleen is sure they must
 lead to somewhere important.

00:17:55.440 --> 00:18:00.846
KATHLEEN: I tried to go inside
but then the, the level is
deeper and I almost fall down,

00:18:03.248 --> 00:18:06.552
so I need to pump
up the water.

00:18:08.219 --> 00:18:11.223
I have to, I have to
explore this door.

00:18:20.064 --> 00:18:24.703
♪ ♪

00:18:26.337 --> 00:18:29.608
(speaking in native language)

00:18:32.043 --> 00:18:35.747
 NARRATOR: Kathleen will need
 to find a water pump before
 she can explore the flooded

00:18:35.780 --> 00:18:38.650
 tunnels any further.

00:18:39.117 --> 00:18:42.888
KATHLEEN: You cannot walk
there, or crawl, because of
the water, it's, it's unsafe.

00:18:44.422 --> 00:18:48.393
It will one of the
greatest adventures in the
excavation now because we

00:18:48.426 --> 00:18:51.830
need to know what is in there.

00:18:52.397 --> 00:18:56.368
 NARRATOR: Kathleen is
 convinced Cleopatra's lost
 tomb is hidden somewhere

00:18:56.401 --> 00:18:58.637
 around this site.

00:18:58.836 --> 00:19:03.709
 She has evidence the
 temple is linked to the
 Egyptian goddess Isis.

00:19:04.075 --> 00:19:07.713
 Kathleen thinks this is
 her biggest clue so far.

00:19:08.313 --> 00:19:12.083
KATHLEEN: We have
archaeological evidence that
the temple was maybe the most

00:19:12.116 --> 00:19:15.654
important religious
center for Isis in the north,

00:19:16.087 --> 00:19:20.292
and the thing we know
about Queen Cleopatra is

00:19:20.325 --> 00:19:23.662
that she was buried
in a temple of Isis.

00:19:24.128 --> 00:19:28.300
So it could be a perfect place
for Cleopatra's lost tomb.

00:19:31.836 --> 00:19:35.541
 NARRATOR: But who was
 Isis, and how is she
 connected to Cleopatra?

00:19:43.014 --> 00:19:48.153
 380 miles south
 of Taposiris Magna on the
 banks of the river Nile,

00:19:49.220 --> 00:19:52.824
 parts of this vast temple
 site are dedicated to Isis,

00:19:53.658 --> 00:19:56.261
 who was a well-loved
 Egyptian goddess in

00:19:56.294 --> 00:19:58.830
 Cleopatra's time.

00:20:00.965 --> 00:20:05.470
 It's here
 that Dr. Colleen Darnell
 continues her own search for

00:20:05.503 --> 00:20:10.075
 clues to Cleopatra's life,
 written in the hieroglyphs.

00:20:11.743 --> 00:20:14.813
COLLEEN: We're walking
to the temple at Dendera,
and one of the most

00:20:14.846 --> 00:20:18.250
significant scenes here is
a depiction of Cleopatra.

00:20:27.325 --> 00:20:30.862
 NARRATOR:
 The temple was first
 built 2,000-years ago and

00:20:30.895 --> 00:20:35.534
 became a major
 place of worship for
 ordinary Egyptians.

00:20:36.067 --> 00:20:37.469
 Through the centuries,

00:20:37.502 --> 00:20:41.239
 a succession
 of pharaohs carved their
 names and images here so

00:20:41.272 --> 00:20:44.610
 they could be worshipped,
 including Cleopatra.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:52.484
COLLEEN: So the title here
is lord of the two lands,

00:20:52.517 --> 00:20:56.989
referring to Upper and
Lower Egypt, Cleo-pat-ra.

00:20:58.756 --> 00:21:02.827
 NARRATOR: Cleopatra
 made a shrewd decision;
 on the temple she wears

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:06.331
 the symbolic headdress of Isis.

00:21:06.531 --> 00:21:11.436
COLLEEN: Here we see the
famous representation of
Cleopatra as Goddess Isis.

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:15.607
Here we have Cleopatra
and her son Caesarion.

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:19.177
So Cleopatra has a long wig,

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:23.248
the horns and sun disk, and
ostrich feathers behind that.

00:21:24.916 --> 00:21:28.920
 NARRATOR: Cleopatra
 wanted to be seen by
 her subjects as the earthly

00:21:28.953 --> 00:21:31.456
 incarnation of Isis.

00:21:31.689 --> 00:21:35.026
 She was making a
 profound connection with
 one of the most popular

00:21:35.059 --> 00:21:37.996
 goddesses of the time.

00:21:39.897 --> 00:21:45.003
 Isis was famed for
 her powers of healing and
 protection and was adored by

00:21:45.036 --> 00:21:47.939
 both Egyptians and Greeks.

00:21:49.807 --> 00:21:55.413
 By immortalizing herself
 as Isis on the temple wall,
 Cleopatra hoped to keep the

00:21:55.446 --> 00:21:59.718
 full support and love of
 her people, and it worked.

00:22:03.154 --> 00:22:07.559
COLLEEN: For Cleopatra
to step into the role of
Isis really proclaimed her

00:22:07.592 --> 00:22:11.163
identity as divine ruler.

00:22:16.267 --> 00:22:18.336
 NARRATOR: At Taposiris Magna,

00:22:18.369 --> 00:22:21.406
 Kathleen thinks
 Cleopatra's Isis
 connection could mean

00:22:21.439 --> 00:22:24.609
 she's buried somewhere
 beneath the temple.

00:22:25.042 --> 00:22:29.981
 Now, the team is pumping
 out the water from the
 flooded underground tunnels,

00:22:30.248 --> 00:22:33.385
 but it's going to take a
 while before she can explore.

00:22:33.818 --> 00:22:36.054
KATHLEEN: It's working.

00:22:36.087 --> 00:22:38.490
Alhamdulillah.

00:22:38.890 --> 00:22:41.226
It's a big relief
to see it working.

00:22:41.259 --> 00:22:45.330
Imagine, today or
tomorrow we, we're going
to be able to, to explore.

00:22:46.063 --> 00:22:48.400
It's so exciting!

00:22:48.433 --> 00:22:52.437
 NARRATOR: Kathleen believes
 Cleopatra could be buried
 in an underground chamber,

00:22:52.470 --> 00:22:54.973
 and the tunnels
 could lead her to it.

00:22:55.006 --> 00:22:58.477
 She originally found
 the location of the shaft
 using radar technology,

00:22:59.677 --> 00:23:02.781
 but with the potential
 for a huge discovery
 just feet away,

00:23:03.448 --> 00:23:05.316
 she has brought
 in more sensitive

00:23:05.349 --> 00:23:08.286
 military-grade equipment to
 look deeper into the rock.

00:23:08.886 --> 00:23:12.924
KATHLEEN: For me the
future of the excavation is
ground-penetrating radar.

00:23:13.791 --> 00:23:17.962
It's a technology that was
used for military purposes,
searching for tunnels and

00:23:17.995 --> 00:23:22.567
searching for cavities, and
this technology is perfect
for what I am looking for.

00:23:24.936 --> 00:23:27.706
So we, we can work here,
make a profile here?

00:23:29.373 --> 00:23:34.312
 NARRATOR: As they move
 the radar scanner along,
 it fires radio wave pulses

00:23:34.345 --> 00:23:37.182
 into the ground.

00:23:40.084 --> 00:23:43.054
MAN: So here we are going about,
about 15 meter depth.

00:23:44.355 --> 00:23:48.026
 NARRATOR: The data from
 the scan will have to be
 sent away for analysis.

00:23:49.393 --> 00:23:52.330
 It should reveal any hollow
 cavities hidden underground,

00:23:53.431 --> 00:23:55.700
 and possibly even the location

00:23:55.733 --> 00:23:58.303
 of Cleopatra's burial chamber.

00:23:58.336 --> 00:24:01.640
KATHLEEN: I always, you
know, so excited about this.

00:24:04.342 --> 00:24:08.880
 NARRATOR: Back at the
 excavation site, everything
 is resting on the team pumping

00:24:08.913 --> 00:24:12.517
 the water from the
 underground tunnels.

00:24:18.256 --> 00:24:20.658
 NARRATOR: While work
 continues at the dig,

00:24:20.691 --> 00:24:22.227
 in Cairo,

00:24:22.260 --> 00:24:25.197
 Kathleen is attending an
 important event.

00:24:26.631 --> 00:24:27.732
WOMAN: It's nice.

00:24:27.765 --> 00:24:29.667
KATHLEEN: It,
what do you think?

00:24:29.700 --> 00:24:31.536
WOMAN: It's nice, oh my God!

00:24:31.569 --> 00:24:35.907
 NARRATOR: At the Egyptian
 Museum, hundreds of Kathleen's
 finds have been chosen

00:24:35.940 --> 00:24:38.643
 to go on display
 for the very first time.

00:24:39.644 --> 00:24:42.847
 They all come from her
 site at Taposiris Magna,

00:24:42.880 --> 00:24:45.784
 unearthed over ten
 years of excavation.

00:24:46.417 --> 00:24:51.456
 Kathleen believes
 each piece adds further weight
 to her theory that Cleopatra

00:24:51.489 --> 00:24:53.758
 could be buried there.

00:24:53.791 --> 00:24:56.862
KATHLEEN: We, we discover
around 200 coins.

00:24:57.795 --> 00:25:03.068
For example, this is a
coin of Queen Cleopatra.

00:25:04.569 --> 00:25:08.773
Can you imagine that I've been
searching for Queen Cleopatra
and this is the first time I

00:25:08.806 --> 00:25:13.478
was face to face with my
heroine, it was a moment
so exciting in excavation.

00:25:15.246 --> 00:25:17.815
Yes, we are going
to change this one.

00:25:17.848 --> 00:25:19.284
WOMAN: This one?
I get it.

00:25:19.317 --> 00:25:21.085
KATHLEEN: For this one, yes.

00:25:21.118 --> 00:25:25.256
I was thinking now,
when I was a kid in the
Dominican Republic and

00:25:25.289 --> 00:25:29.995
I dream one day to
make discoveries in Egypt,

00:25:31.062 --> 00:25:33.531
and everybody in Dominican,

00:25:33.564 --> 00:25:37.268
my teachers, my parents,
told me this will never happen,

00:25:37.301 --> 00:25:41.473
and now we are
presenting 350 objects.

00:25:52.049 --> 00:25:55.587
 NARRATOR: For
 someone who started as
 an amateur archaeologist,

00:25:55.620 --> 00:26:00.358
 Kathleen now has the eyes of
 the world looking at her finds.

00:26:01.158 --> 00:26:04.262
KATHLEEN: We had a
desire to change history.

00:26:04.662 --> 00:26:08.934
It's one of the greatest
moments in my life.

00:26:09.867 --> 00:26:15.073
Of course, the exhibition,
it's only a presentation
of work, but the real work,

00:26:15.106 --> 00:26:19.678
the one we're really excited
about, is to be onsite and,
and continue searching.

00:26:25.650 --> 00:26:29.387
 NARRATOR: Back at
 the dig site, there's a
 problem with the water pump.

00:26:35.026 --> 00:26:36.428
KATHLEEN: Mohamed,
what happened?

00:26:40.364 --> 00:26:42.500
KATHLEEN: Cut?
MOHAMED Cut, yeah.

00:26:42.833 --> 00:26:43.935
KATHLEEN: It's
not working now?

00:26:46.370 --> 00:26:49.341
KATHLEEN: Can you imagine
after all this effort
now there's no electricity

00:26:49.540 --> 00:26:54.012
in the area, and only a
few hours left today and next,

00:26:54.979 --> 00:26:57.281
and tomorrow, that's it.

00:26:57.314 --> 00:27:00.985
 NARRATOR: Kathleen's
 government permit to
 dig at the site only lasts

00:27:01.018 --> 00:27:03.521
 for one more day.

00:27:03.554 --> 00:27:07.258
 She's now racing against
 the clock to explore
 the underground tunnels.

00:27:08.926 --> 00:27:14.633
KATHLEEN: We face so many
challenges, but we don't,
we, we never give up.

00:27:24.809 --> 00:27:28.647
 NARRATOR: At the
 4,000-year old necropolis
 of Qubbet el-Hawa...

00:27:29.080 --> 00:27:30.882
(speaking in native language).

00:27:30.915 --> 00:27:34.852
 NARRATOR: Alejandro's
 team has unearthed a very
 rare death mask made of a

00:27:34.885 --> 00:27:37.355
 material called cartonnage.

00:27:37.655 --> 00:27:41.926
 He hopes the mask will
 tell him the name of the
 person buried in the tomb,

00:27:42.560 --> 00:27:46.297
 but decoding the hieroglyphs
 is proving difficult.

00:27:47.364 --> 00:27:50.635
ALEJANDRO: I cannot
read properly the,
the, all the signs.

00:27:51.535 --> 00:27:55.740
It will be
better to do it after the
consolidation and cleaning.

00:27:58.142 --> 00:28:01.679
 NARRATOR: Alejandro's
 team has started
 the painstaking process of

00:28:01.712 --> 00:28:03.982
 extracting the mask.

00:28:05.149 --> 00:28:08.186
 Their job is made even
 harder because it's embedded

00:28:08.219 --> 00:28:10.722
 under the bones of its owner.

00:28:10.755 --> 00:28:16.728
ALEJANDRO: It's quite a
delicate moment because we
have human remains that are

00:28:17.228 --> 00:28:20.565
touching and we don't want
to destroy the cartonnage.

00:28:23.434 --> 00:28:26.604
MARTINA: They are taking
off the cartonnage.

00:28:28.906 --> 00:28:31.175
 NARRATOR: The ancient
 mask is carefully removed,

00:28:31.208 --> 00:28:34.912
 but comes out in
 several parts, held
 together with resin and

00:28:34.945 --> 00:28:37.515
 paper to prevent
 any further damage.

00:28:38.115 --> 00:28:40.551
MARTINA: It is really amazing.

00:28:40.584 --> 00:28:42.754
(speaking in native language).

00:28:43.954 --> 00:28:46.157
And I'm simply now checking
if there was name or not.

00:28:46.190 --> 00:28:49.160
Yes, there are
more hieroglyphs.

00:28:50.027 --> 00:28:56.367
ALEJANDRO: Here is
the name, it's for the
soul of Seti Hacaib a Inet.

00:28:58.035 --> 00:29:01.106
 NARRATOR: Alejandro
 can now put a name
 to the unknown body,

00:29:02.106 --> 00:29:06.077
 but he still doesn't
 know the persons job,
 or role in society.

00:29:06.944 --> 00:29:10.715
ALEJANDRO: We have
now to look in the, in
the publications to see

00:29:10.748 --> 00:29:15.753
if we have any reference
in the neighborhood or
in other documents,

00:29:15.786 --> 00:29:18.857
and but it, it's amazing.

00:29:19.390 --> 00:29:24.295
 NARRATOR: The death mask
 is now taken to their on-site
 lab for further analysis.

00:29:24.929 --> 00:29:29.300
 The team will try to
 piece it back together
 like a jigsaw puzzle.

00:29:29.333 --> 00:29:33.938
 There could still be more
 secrets to be revealed
 about this mysterious man.

00:29:38.909 --> 00:29:42.914
 In Aswan, on the
 other side of the site,
 Alejandro has unearthed

00:29:42.947 --> 00:29:46.384
 several mummies still intact.

00:29:46.417 --> 00:29:50.254
 He's searching for
 clues to their identity,
 which may lie hidden within

00:29:50.287 --> 00:29:52.523
 the ancient bandages,

00:29:52.556 --> 00:29:56.594
 but to keep
 them intact archaeologists
 are no longer allowed to

00:29:56.627 --> 00:29:59.163
 open up the wrappings.

00:29:59.196 --> 00:30:02.901
ALEJANDRO: 100 years
ago it was common just
to cut the wrappings.

00:30:03.834 --> 00:30:10.108
Today we are lucky to
have non-invasive techniques,
and the idea is that we are

00:30:10.941 --> 00:30:17.348
going to take to the university
hospital in Aswan where they
have very good CT scans.

00:30:20.451 --> 00:30:25.657
 NARRATOR: By scanning the
 bodies, Alejandro hopes to
 examine how they died, and

00:30:25.890 --> 00:30:29.661
 also to see if
 there are any funerary
 objects hidden inside.

00:30:30.227 --> 00:30:34.932
ALEJANDRO: We have the
possibility that he could have
a dagger or a metal object

00:30:34.965 --> 00:30:41.372
inside, we could confirm
the age of death, if he
suffer any kind of disease.

00:30:42.339 --> 00:30:45.143
Definitely the CT scan will
tell us a lot of information.

00:30:52.216 --> 00:30:56.787
 NARRATOR: In the Valley of
 the Kings, John and Colleen
 Darnell continue their search

00:30:56.820 --> 00:31:01.125
 for clues to Cleopatra's
 life and untimely death.

00:31:02.760 --> 00:31:07.865
 Deep in the tomb of Pharaoh
 Seti I the first, they're
 examining inscriptions that

00:31:07.898 --> 00:31:13.438
 could shed light on
 how Cleopatra chose
 to commit suicide.

00:31:22.212 --> 00:31:24.448
 The tombs of the
 Valley of the Kings were

00:31:24.481 --> 00:31:27.652
 built during a golden age
 in Egyptian civilization.

00:31:29.219 --> 00:31:32.623
 Treasures and
 decorations reveal
 the symbolism that played

00:31:32.656 --> 00:31:35.326
 a key role in
 their belief system.

00:31:35.893 --> 00:31:40.899
 The tomb of Pharaoh
 Seti the first lies in the
 southeast of the Valley,

00:31:41.198 --> 00:31:44.335
 it's the deepest and most
 widely decorated.

00:31:44.969 --> 00:31:49.407
 Painted on its walls
 are images of gods and
 goddesses who lay at the

00:31:49.440 --> 00:31:52.343
 heart of Egyptian society.

00:31:52.609 --> 00:31:56.514
 Forming a belief
 system that continued
 until Cleopatra's time.

00:32:00.417 --> 00:32:04.322
COLLEEN: Here deep in
the tomb of Seti I we
see a fantastic depiction of

00:32:04.355 --> 00:32:06.424
the goddess Wadjet,

00:32:06.924 --> 00:32:10.895
she's labelled here in
the hieroglyphs and she
is the cobra who sits on the

00:32:10.928 --> 00:32:12.697
brow of the king.

00:32:12.730 --> 00:32:16.634
 NARRATOR: Wadjet was
 the protector of Egypt
 and of its pharaohs.

00:32:16.667 --> 00:32:20.238
 She often took the form
 of a snake, usually
 an Egyptian cobra.

00:32:21.805 --> 00:32:26.411
 Legend has it that Cleopatra
 killed herself with the
 bite of a venomous snake

00:32:26.944 --> 00:32:30.181
 when trapped by the
 invading Roman army.

00:32:30.447 --> 00:32:35.152
COLLEEN: This depiction is
over 1,000 years before the
suicide of Cleopatra, and the

00:32:35.185 --> 00:32:39.691
fact that she chooses
this ancient symbol of the
pharaohs, the asp, the cobra,

00:32:40.424 --> 00:32:44.395
to commit suicide,
she's taking the
ultimate royal symbol,

00:32:45.129 --> 00:32:50.268
she wants to be linked in
to the earlier, the deep,
ancient past of Egypt.

00:32:52.503 --> 00:32:55.806
 NARRATOR: Cleopatra,
 through her life and death,

00:32:55.839 --> 00:32:59.310
 was obsessed with the
 traditions of ancient Egypt.

00:33:02.980 --> 00:33:07.351
 At Taposiris Magna,
 Kathleen believes she's
 getting ever closer to

00:33:07.384 --> 00:33:10.288
 finding Cleopatra's lost tomb.

00:33:11.055 --> 00:33:14.658
 As the dig season is
 coming to an end, she's
 desperate to see if the

00:33:14.691 --> 00:33:18.262
 underground tunnels lead to
 a burial chamber.

00:33:19.797 --> 00:33:20.932
KATHLEEN: Is it working?

00:33:23.700 --> 00:33:27.338
 NARRATOR: Her team
 has now been pumping
 out water for two days,

00:33:27.371 --> 00:33:30.475
 but power cuts have
 severely hindered progress.

00:33:34.411 --> 00:33:39.617
KATHLEEN: Maybe we, we can,
I can go down and try to
see and I will explore.

00:33:43.620 --> 00:33:45.189
MAN: Shall we start?

00:33:45.222 --> 00:33:48.926
KATHLEEN: Uh-huh.
I am ready.

00:33:52.529 --> 00:33:54.031
Okay.

00:33:54.064 --> 00:33:55.666
MAN: Bye bye.

00:34:10.180 --> 00:34:13.785
 NARRATOR: This is the
 first time Kathleen has been
 able to explore the tunnels.

00:34:19.523 --> 00:34:23.194
 NARRATOR: She starts
 with the one leading
 away from the temple.

00:34:50.053 --> 00:34:54.058
 NARRATOR: With the
 way forward still flooded
 Kathleen has to turn back.

00:34:55.592 --> 00:34:58.162
 She now explores
 the second tunnel.

00:35:44.041 --> 00:35:46.877
 NARRATOR: These
 tunnels would have taken
 months or even years to

00:35:46.910 --> 00:35:48.913
 carve out by hand.

00:35:49.379 --> 00:35:51.682
KATHLEEN: Uh! Alhamdulillah.

00:35:52.482 --> 00:35:53.951
MAN: Hamdulillah.

00:35:53.984 --> 00:35:56.554
 NARRATOR: Kathleen
 believes they must lead
 somewhere important.

00:35:56.587 --> 00:36:00.191
KATHLEEN: It was incredible.

00:36:00.624 --> 00:36:06.397
Now we know a lot about
this shaft, unfortunately
we could not see the

00:36:07.431 --> 00:36:11.135
end of this tunnel,
there was a lot of water.

00:36:11.368 --> 00:36:14.738
 NARRATOR: With her
 permit about to expire,
 Kathleen's excavation must

00:36:14.771 --> 00:36:16.507
 come to an end,

00:36:16.540 --> 00:36:19.777
 but there is still a
 chance that the data from
 the ground-penetrating

00:36:19.810 --> 00:36:23.781
 radar might reveal if the
 tunnels lead to a tomb.

00:36:24.448 --> 00:36:28.052
KATHLEEN: Now we are
waiting for the GPR results,

00:36:28.485 --> 00:36:31.589
so I have to be
patient and, and wait.

00:36:42.432 --> 00:36:46.704
 NARRATOR: In Aswan,
 Alejandro is preparing
 for a night-time mission.

00:36:47.304 --> 00:36:51.976
 He's about to transport six
 ancient mummies across the
 city to a local hospital.

00:36:53.510 --> 00:36:57.381
 He's arranged to use
 their medical scanner
 after hours to see what may

00:36:57.414 --> 00:37:00.251
 lie hidden inside
 these ancient bodies.

00:37:06.423 --> 00:37:09.894
 NARRATOR: For security,
 a police escort
 joins the convoy.

00:37:20.737 --> 00:37:26.744
To try to know something
about how they were buried,

00:37:27.144 --> 00:37:30.681
the pathologies,
the possible diseases
that they suffer,

00:37:30.714 --> 00:37:33.684
the cause of death, gender, age.

00:37:33.917 --> 00:37:36.920
 NARRATOR: The C-T
 scanner should be able to
 see through the wrappings

00:37:36.953 --> 00:37:38.589
 to the bones below,

00:37:38.622 --> 00:37:42.560
 but Alejandro is still
 worried about damaging
 the fragile remains.

00:37:43.260 --> 00:37:45.629
ALEJANDRO: Mummies
are very delicate,

00:37:45.662 --> 00:37:49.300
so you have to
think that they,
they have been wrapped

00:37:49.333 --> 00:37:51.702
more than 2,000 years ago,

00:37:52.502 --> 00:37:54.772
so they might
suffer damages.

00:37:55.372 --> 00:37:57.808
Well, let's go.

00:38:00.177 --> 00:38:01.945
Hello?

00:38:01.978 --> 00:38:03.546
Inshallah.

00:38:03.580 --> 00:38:07.718
We, yeah, yeah, yeah,
we, we will arrive in five,
ten minutes maximum, okay?

00:38:08.085 --> 00:38:09.620
Ooph.

00:38:11.355 --> 00:38:15.426
We have to, to take
this opportunity to get as
much information as possible,

00:38:16.927 --> 00:38:19.263
so we will see.

00:38:22.566 --> 00:38:26.437
 NARRATOR: Alejandro's
 night-time activities have
 attracted the attention

00:38:26.470 --> 00:38:28.639
 of the local press.

00:38:29.539 --> 00:38:34.378
ALEJANDRO: I will ask
to the journalists please
to leave to the specialists

00:38:34.411 --> 00:38:36.347
to make their work.

00:38:36.380 --> 00:38:38.349
MAN: Please, which one we
will start now, which one?

00:38:38.382 --> 00:38:40.117
ALEJANDRO: Yeah, this one.

00:38:40.150 --> 00:38:42.787
MAN: Thank you, okay.

00:38:43.587 --> 00:38:44.655
You're ready?

00:38:44.688 --> 00:38:46.890
ALEJANDRO: Yes.

00:38:46.923 --> 00:38:50.561
 NARRATOR: The mummies
 are wrapped in cloth for added
 protection inside the scanner.

00:38:52.162 --> 00:38:56.433
 It works by taking
 a series of x-rays at
 different angles to create

00:38:56.466 --> 00:38:58.569
 a three-dimensional
 image of the body.

00:39:02.539 --> 00:39:06.510
ALEJANDRO: We are
just checking if the
scan was done right.

00:39:06.810 --> 00:39:09.980
 NARRATOR: So far, very little
 is known about these mummies,

00:39:10.013 --> 00:39:13.117
 like how they died,
 and whether they were
 old or young.

00:39:13.850 --> 00:39:17.054
 Alejandro is
 trying to piece
 together their identities,

00:39:17.087 --> 00:39:20.391
 hoping to discover
 any new clues to make
 sense of their lives,

00:39:21.057 --> 00:39:22.860
 and ultimately,
 their deaths.

00:39:26.029 --> 00:39:29.900
The first analysis
of the body shows that he
was over 60 when he died.

00:39:32.102 --> 00:39:34.739
So now I have to choose
who is going to be the next.

00:39:36.873 --> 00:39:38.809
Okay? Let's go.

00:39:43.547 --> 00:39:46.617
Well, now we have
something very interesting.

00:39:48.051 --> 00:39:53.090
Interpreted that the mummy
was going to be a man, but
it seems that it is a woman.

00:39:54.191 --> 00:39:57.094
We didn't, we
didn't expect that.

00:40:00.997 --> 00:40:03.300
 NARRATOR: As the final
 body enters the scanner,

00:40:03.333 --> 00:40:05.936
 the archaeologists
 spot something amazing.

00:40:09.573 --> 00:40:11.275
WOMAN: Si.

00:40:11.975 --> 00:40:13.710
ALEJANDRO: We have amulets.

00:40:13.743 --> 00:40:16.814
Together with the scarab,
a wing, winged scarab.

00:40:18.014 --> 00:40:19.516
MAN: Sign of Horus.

00:40:19.549 --> 00:40:21.084
ALEJANDRO: Ah-ha.

00:40:21.117 --> 00:40:23.454
(speaking in native language).

00:40:23.687 --> 00:40:28.392
 NARRATOR: The scan reveals
 an elaborate carved amulet in
 the shape of a scarab beetle.

00:40:29.693 --> 00:40:34.398
 Funerary amulets were often
 used by the elite to protect
 the soul of the deceased,

00:40:35.966 --> 00:40:38.736
 and the scarab beetle
 symbolized rebirth.

00:40:41.071 --> 00:40:45.642
 The scarab was placed
 over the position of the
 heart and often had spells

00:40:45.675 --> 00:40:47.778
 written on it.

00:40:48.411 --> 00:40:52.716
 These spells gave
 instructions to the person's
 heart to help them during the

00:40:52.749 --> 00:40:54.985
 judgement of their soul.

00:40:58.989 --> 00:41:04.128
ALEJANDRO: It's the first time
that I can see them in the,
in the position in,

00:41:04.594 --> 00:41:07.364
in its position in the
body, so, exciting.

00:41:08.265 --> 00:41:12.002
 NARRATOR: Out of the
 nine mummies Alejandro's
 team have scanned,

00:41:12.035 --> 00:41:16.607
 this is the only one to
 have an amulet still
 in its original position.

00:41:17.440 --> 00:41:22.213
 With such a precious
 find, Alejandro can wrap
 up his night on a high.

00:41:23.980 --> 00:41:28.385
ALEJANDRO: Now it's 12:00 and,
hmm, I'm completely exhausted.

00:41:33.623 --> 00:41:35.359
Thank you.

00:41:38.528 --> 00:41:40.330
 NARRATOR: At Taposiris Magna,

00:41:40.363 --> 00:41:44.535
 Kathleen has received
 news about her radar
 search for Cleopatra's tomb.

00:41:45.702 --> 00:41:49.706
KATHLEEN: Today is the
last day and the people which
are doing the, the radar,

00:41:49.739 --> 00:41:52.576
they're bringing the result and
they just told me,

00:41:53.076 --> 00:41:56.080
"We have great news for you."

00:42:01.318 --> 00:42:05.689
So tell me what is
the good news we have?

00:42:14.798 --> 00:42:16.634
KATHLEEN: Possible chamber?
MAN: Yes.

00:42:17.100 --> 00:42:20.638
KATHLEEN: Wow.
MAN: Yes.
KATHLEEN: I'm going to cry.

00:42:22.238 --> 00:42:25.342
Really, I'm trying to,
I'm so happy.

00:42:27.043 --> 00:42:31.315
It could be anything buried
there but I feel it's,
it's what I'm looking for.

00:42:34.718 --> 00:42:39.122
 NARRATOR: Kathleen's scans
 reveal a thirty-foot-wide
 cavity directly beneath the

00:42:39.155 --> 00:42:41.425
 entrance to the temple.

00:42:42.792 --> 00:42:49.099
 It would have taken ancient
 workers a monumental effort to
 build, and if it's a tomb it

00:42:49.566 --> 00:42:52.469
 must be the tomb of
 someone important.

00:42:55.505 --> 00:43:01.545
 This could be the perfect
 hiding place for the last
 queen of Egypt, Cleopatra.

00:43:02.112 --> 00:43:06.683
 The tomb could hold her
 royal treasures, and its
 discovery would be one of

00:43:06.716 --> 00:43:10.888
 the greatest finds in the
 history of archaeology.

00:43:12.222 --> 00:43:14.725
KATHLEEN: So the
room is big, and this...

00:43:14.758 --> 00:43:18.996
MAN: Ten meters.
KATHLEEN: Ten meters long? Wow.
MAN: Yeah.

00:43:20.063 --> 00:43:24.568
 NARRATOR: For Kathleen,
 Cleopatra's lost tomb could
 now be within her grasp.

00:43:26.636 --> 00:43:29.573
KATHLEEN: I'm just really
excited and I'm touched.

00:43:30.073 --> 00:43:33.577
This is something that is
really important, precious,
something very precious they

00:43:33.610 --> 00:43:35.545
tried to hide there.

00:43:35.578 --> 00:43:39.450
So I think this is the
final stage of my search.

00:43:42.185 --> 00:43:45.623
 NARRATOR: It's been
 an incredible season for
 Kathleen and her workers,

00:43:46.589 --> 00:43:48.759
 but with her
 permit now expired,

00:43:48.792 --> 00:43:53.397
 she must secure the
 site and continue her search
 for the chamber next year.

00:43:54.230 --> 00:43:56.233
KATHLEEN: Next season
I will come back.

00:43:56.266 --> 00:44:00.037
This is the moment
that I was waiting for.

00:44:01.237 --> 00:44:05.175
Now I know exactly
where to continue.

00:44:10.080 --> 00:44:11.081
 

